From 432ea991ceb05d33435edbb9f1352526ee8382a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DisplayXR <dev@displayxr.invalid>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 16:24:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] inline-3d(#159): retract inline-3D rects when the widget is
 hidden, not only on commit

Going Back weaves the previous page's tile region over the restored page's
ordinary 2D content, for a while, then heals by itself.

0058 (#87) already clears the rects on navigation, and its comment names Back
explicitly -- but it hooks WebFrameWidgetImpl::DidNavigate(), which is called
from LocalFrameClientImpl::DispatchDidCommitLoad, i.e. only on a navigation
COMMIT. Two common paths never commit:

  1. Back/forward cache. Going Back does not commit the outgoing document, it
     freezes it into the bfcache ALIVE. Nothing clears its rects, and because a
     frozen page runs no rAF it never pushes the empty set that would. The
     rects stay latched downstream and the restored page's 2D content is woven
     where the tile used to be. It heals when the entry is evicted -- hence
     "for some time" rather than "forever", which is the detail that pointed
     here.
  2. Tab switch. Switching to a 2D tab commits nothing, so a background 3D tab
     keeps its rects latched and the panel stays in 3D.

Clear on WasHidden() instead: a widget that is not being shown must not be
claiming panel real estate, and hiding is the one signal both paths share.
Self-correcting by construction -- 0058's contract that "a new inline-3d
session re-reports its rects on its first frame" still holds, and WasShown()
resumes rAF, so a spurious hide costs at most one flat frame.

The rect state is separate from the display-mode wish: 0066 (#90) already made
the WISH bfcache-aware via PrimaryPageChanged, which is why the panel's 2D/3D
demand retracts correctly while the woven rects did not. This gives the rect
half the same property.
---
 .../core/frame/web_frame_widget_impl.cc       | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/web_frame_widget_impl.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/web_frame_widget_impl.cc
index f61dfc5..31f8b14 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/web_frame_widget_impl.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/web_frame_widget_impl.cc
@@ -5415,6 +5415,30 @@ WebFrameWidgetImpl::ScreenOrientationOverride() {
 }
 
 void WebFrameWidgetImpl::WasHidden() {
+  // browser#159: retract this widget's inline-3D rects the moment it stops
+  // being shown. DidNavigate() (browser#87, above) covers a navigation COMMIT,
+  // which is the only place the rects were cleared — and two very common paths
+  // never reach it:
+  //
+  //   1. BACK/FORWARD CACHE. DidNavigate() is called from
+  //      LocalFrameClientImpl::DispatchDidCommitLoad, i.e. on a commit. Going
+  //      Back does not commit this document; it FREEZES it into the bfcache
+  //      alive, so nothing here runs. The last rects it pushed stay latched
+  //      downstream (a frozen page runs no rAF, so it never pushes the empty
+  //      set that would clear them), and the page the user lands on gets its
+  //      ordinary 2D content woven wherever the 3D tile used to be. It
+  //      self-heals only when the entry is evicted, which is why the report
+  //      was "for some time" rather than "forever".
+  //   2. TAB SWITCH. Switching to a 2D tab commits nothing at all, so a
+  //      background 3D tab kept its rects latched and the panel stayed in 3D.
+  //
+  // Hiding is the honest common signal: a widget that is not being shown must
+  // not be claiming panel real estate. Clearing is safe and self-correcting —
+  // 0058's contract still holds, that "a new inline-3d session re-reports its
+  // rects on its first frame", and WasShown() resumes rAF. The worst case on a
+  // spurious hide is one flat frame before the next rAF re-reports.
+  SetInline3DRects(std::vector<gfx::Rect>(), gfx::PointF());
+
   ForEachLocalFrameControlledByWidget(local_root_->GetFrame(),
                                       [](WebLocalFrameImpl* local_frame) {
                                         local_frame->Client()->WasHidden();
-- 
